Sources

1. Human Reference Atlas 3D reference objects (HuBMAP CCF), the Visible
   Human male and female, release v2.0: models/3d-vh-m-united.glb.zip and
   models/3d-vh-f-united.glb.7z (https://github.com/hubmapconsortium/ccf-releases).
   3D reference organs by Kristen Browne (3D modeller) and Katy Börner, HuBMAP
   CCF; described in Herr BW II, Hardi J, Quardokus EM, Bueckle A, Chen L,
   Wang F, Caron AR, Osumi-Sutherland D, Musen MA, Börner K. Specimen,
   biological structure, and spatial ontologies in support of a Human
   Reference Atlas. Sci Data. 2023;10:171. doi:10.1038/s41597-023-01993-8.
   Licensed CC BY 4.0
   (https://github.com/hubmapconsortium/ccf-3d-reference-object-library).
   Derived from the Visible Human Project data: Courtesy of the U.S. National
   Library of Medicine.

2. The brain in every file (the HRA's "Allen_brain" node) is the Allen Human
   Reference Atlas – 3D, 2020: Ding S-L, Royall JJ, Sunkin SM, Facer BAC,
   Lesnar P, Bernard A, Ng L, Lein ES. Allen Human Reference Atlas – 3D, 2020.
   RRID:SCR_017764, version 1.0.0. © 2019 Allen Institute for Brain Science.
   Licensed CC BY 4.0 (from 1 September 2022).

3. The children's outlines (boy.glb, girl.glb, the "skin" mesh) are made from
   the MakeHuman base mesh and macro targets, CC0 1.0
   (makehumancommunity/makehuman at a8bc2d54ff0ac92e78ff71431b1023eda42bf482).

Changes

- Each body is cut into one mesh per region and side, as named in
  src/body/regions.ts, plus one mesh each for the skin, the rest of the
  skeleton and the thymus.
- Other structures (eyes, vessels, nerves, lymph node, reproductive organs,
  larynx, bronchi) are left out.
- The meshes are welded, simplified with meshoptimizer, quantised and
  meshopt-compressed by tools/body/build.mjs.
- boy.glb and girl.glb are the male and female interiors moved and resized,
  organ by organ, to paediatric reference measurements
  (components/body/references.json). They are fitted inside the MakeHuman
  outline, with growth plates and the pelvis's seams drawn as cartilage.

